  <result aggregation-status="0" type="2">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output 1.4. Strengthened social dialogue and labour relations laws, processes and institutions</narrative>
   </title>
   <description>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Department of Labour, Government of Telangana has enhanced its labour dispute resolution capacity through training of its six officials on conciliation/mediation.
 1. An assessment of the labour dispute resolution system in the state of Telangana commenced in 2021. The ITC-Turin Centre provided training to labour officials in the State. 
2. Tripartite social dialogue mechanisms at Centre and State levels, and their roles in responding to the COVID-19 crisis documented by the ILO. The collation in the form of the &quot;Towards resilient social dialogue in South Asia&quot; report was developed in consultation with the tripartite constituents. The report was published in October 2020. This is the first such collation that has been developed for India. It provided constituents with comprehensive information on each of the key tripartite social dialogue mechanisms that have been established in India; including in respect of composition, mandates, challenges and the manner in which they have responded to the COVID-19 pandemic.
3. The Towards resilient social dialogue in South Asia report published in October 2020, prioritises the need to strengthen social dialogue in the informal economy. To this end, a research initiative was initiated in India in 2021 by the ILO. The research initiative aims to identify strategies and tools to strengthen organising by employers&apos; organisations and trade unions in respect of India&apos;s informal economy.  
4. The ILO has compiled a briefing note on social dialogue mechanisms in the state of Karnataka. The briefing note provides information on the tripartite social dialogue mechanisms, relevant legislation and the status of tripartite social dialogue mechanisms in Karnataka. The note is aimed to inform initiatives to strengthen social dialogue in this State.</narrative>
   </description>
